{"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Make the destination with one of the factories, which fill in the endpoint, the credentials’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"header field, this encoder and its limits:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let segment = try HTTPDestination.segment(","    writeKey: writeKey,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the workspace is","    plan: plan)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body is a JSON object of content type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application\/json"},{"type":"text","text":" with one member, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch"},{"type":"text","text":", an array"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of track calls, one per record, oldest first, with these members:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymousId"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; the record’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" when its context has no session"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"context","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The standard context, in the spec’s field names (below), and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"0.0.0.0\""}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event\/name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as it is","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"messageId"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s stored properties, by name"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"request_ip"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"0.0.0.0\""},{"text":", in RudderStack’s calls alone","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the event was tracked, in ISO 8601 with milliseconds, in UTC"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"type"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"\"track\"","type":"codeVoice"}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userId"},{"type":"text","text":", no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identify"},{"type":"text","text":" call, no traits,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context.device.id"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"advertisingId"},{"type":"text","text":". An endpoint counts a user per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymousId"},{"type":"text","text":", so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its anonymous users are sessions. A record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions()"},{"type":"text","text":", or one a store recovered after a relaunch, which keeps no context) is its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own anonymous user, linked to nothing: the spec rejects a call with neither a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userId"},{"type":"text","text":" nor an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymousId"},{"type":"text","text":". Segment deduplicates calls by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"messageId"},{"type":"text","text":" over about the last 24 hours, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drops most duplicates rather than all, so a recovered record Segment had already stored before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the app ended is most likely not stored again, whatever its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymousId"},{"type":"text","text":". RudderStack’s and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Customer.io’s references don’t say whether they deduplicate. The record’s vendor identifier"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and trace context, and any other context value, aren’t sent."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context.ip"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"0.0.0.0\""},{"type":"text","text":" in every call, which the spec reads as the user’s address, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Segment records no address from the request. RudderStack fills in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"request_ip"},{"type":"text","text":" member from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the request unless the call has one, even when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context.ip"},{"type":"text","text":" is set, and passes it on to its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destinations, so RudderStack’s calls also carry "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"request_ip"},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"0.0.0.0\""},{"type":"text","text":". Customer.io’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"references don’t say whether "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context.ip"},{"type":"text","text":" takes the place of the address it reads from an HTTP"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request. No call to Segment or Customer.io carries "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"request_ip"},{"type":"text","text":", which their specs don’t have."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sentAt"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"originalTimestamp"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"channel"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent. Without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sentAt"},{"type":"text","text":" the endpoint takes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"},{"type":"text","text":" as it is, uncorrected for the device’s clock; it is left out on purpose, as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"retried request sends the same body again, whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sentAt"},{"type":"text","text":" would be the first attempt’s."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"RudderStack, whose references list all three as required, fills them in from when it received"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the call."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyReader"},{"text":" reads them. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","type":"reference"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, an element of an array is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context"},{"text":" holds these members, for each of the keys the record’s context has a value for:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Key","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"app","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplicationKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"namespace","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the bundle identifier, ","type":"text"},{"code":"version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"build","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", each left out when ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; no ","type":"text"},{"code":"app","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when all three are","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"DeviceKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"model"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"type"},{"type":"text","text":", the platform as Segment’s Swift library names it: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ios"},{"type":"text","text":" for a phone or pad, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"macos"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tvos"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"watchos"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"visionos"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"locale"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocaleKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The locale’s BCP 47 identifier, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"en-US"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"network","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"NetworkKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"wifi"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cellular"},{"type":"text","text":", whether the connection is each"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"os","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"OperatingSystemKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sent: one whose event and version ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name is one of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Customer.io’s semantic events, which delete or suppress people and devices, one whose event","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"isn’t ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no ISO 8601 form,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and one too large for a call (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecEncodingError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"). ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" returns them as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"text":"s, which ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" logs and reports on its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing for it. A record sent again keeps its "},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The bytes are the same for the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records on every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"UTF-8 bytes."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/segmentspecbatchencoder"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"},"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" of the Segment spec’s batch call, so an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can send events to Segment, RudderStack, Customer.io Data Pipelines, or another endpoint that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"takes Segment’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/v1\/batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","title":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder.swift#L90"},"externalID":"s:19SegmentSpecEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV","modules":[{"name":"SegmentSpecEncoding"}],"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[